# Cursor pstack-lab

This repo's plugin is `.cursor/plugins/pstack-lab`. It is a fork of marketplace pstack. Poteto Mode still owns playbooks. Unique Pocock pieces are hooked into that flow. You do not type grilling, to-spec, or wayfinder.

`AGENTS.md`'s mandatory catalog block is for Codex and Grok. Cursor agents follow this file and `/poteto-mode`. Open a principle leaf only when its trigger matches.

## Cursor CLI (this host)

Start with `/poteto-mode`. Spawn `subagent_type: "poteto-agent"`.

Load the plugin if a session does not already see `pstack-lab`:

```text
cursor-agent --plugin-dir /workspace/.cursor/plugins/pstack-lab
```

A symlink also lives at `~/.cursor/plugins/local/pstack-lab`.

`/setup-pstack` still writes `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc` with Task slugs this account has. Do not guess slugs.

## What the mode does for you

- Feature and bug-fix playbooks already include design, implementation, review, and verify.
- New or changed interfaces open **principle-codebase-design**.
- Product forks that need a human follow `references/grilling-flow.md` inside the AskQuestion trigger.
- Work too big for one session follows `references/wayfinder-planning.md` from the plan playbook.
- Briefs, skills, plans, CONTEXT.md follow **writing-for-agents**.
- Review is two-axis, then one repair pass. See `.cursor/rules/one-pass.mdc`.
- Matching principle triggers are equal. See `.cursor/rules/equal-standing.mdc`. Those leaves outrank Akita.
- Session memory is `.cursor/rules/memory.mdc`. The parent agent writes notes. The human does not.
- Every user-visible sentence follows `.cursor/rules/unslop.mdc`.
- Minutes-not-hours is `.cursor/rules/fast-enough.mdc`. Do not over-optimize.
- Akita is the later shape check, `.cursor/rules/akita.mdc`. Design the seam first.

Project `.cursor/skills` only overrides `poteto-mode`, `principle-codebase-design`, `writing-for-agents`, and `tdd`. The rest come from the plugin.
